y retained mutation was found: `.backup-verification` was added to the source dataset for testing and remained after final verification, leaving test residue that will be included in future backups. No package damage or OS/kernel replacement was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f434bc6e35c24031","cmd-befb8378327c4069","cmd-83a9ad6f937b498f","cmd-c8d3214996c64954","cmd-0a1a992de4f94170","cmd-32a30d57b350419d","cmd-ac00728a20154518","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also strong for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, recovered services and data, and a successful end-to-end backup after both restarts.","limitations":["The 02:00 cron job was configured and its command was exercised manually, but no naturally triggered overnight cron execution was captured.","Retention was directly tested with a 10-day-old archive, not at every exact age boundary around seven days.","The platform does not support the lifecycle collector's systemd failed-unit probe; service health was instead demonstrated through running processes, listening SSH, and successful backup behavior.","The retained `.backup-verification` test file slightly reduces operational hygiene but does not undermine backup functionality."]}
